, "top": [[" **", -0.0005024741403758526], ["**", -9.230891227722168]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -3.862455560010858e-05, "top": [["`", -3.862455560010858e-05], ["```", -12.520180702209473]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -6.616334576392546e-05, "top": [["ic", -6.616334576392546e-05], [" ic", -11.132599830627441]]}, {"t": "px", "lp": -0.00012672750744968653, "top": [["px", -0.00012672750744968653], ["xx", -11.133245468139648]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.0004415891016833484, "top": [["`", -0.0004415891016833484], [" `", -9.295449256896973]]}, {"t": "**", "lp": -0.00041666364995762706, "top": [["**", -0.00041666364995762706], ["**:", -8.82105827331543]]}, {"t": " :", "lp": -7.665451266802847e-05, "top": [[" :", -7.665451266802847e-05], [" **", -11.365005493164062]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line, explaining each flag and its purpose.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag ensures it works even if already sourced. Without this, `icx`/`icpx` wouldn't be found.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nStops the build immediately if any command fails (non-zero exit). Essential for catching errors early.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S` : **source directory** (where the source code lives)\n- `-B` : **build directory** (where compilation output goes)\n- `-G Ninja` : Use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, efficient build system)\n\n## Build Configuration Flags\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimized build with compiler optimizations enabled (`-O3`), no debug symbols.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- Install prefix: `/usr` (standard system location)\n- Library directory: `lib` (not `lib64`, important for Arch's multiarch layout)\n\n## Compiler Selection\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx\n```\nUse Intel's compilers:\n- **`icx`** : Intel oneAPI DPC++/C compiler (for C code)\n- **`icpx`** :"}